 <h2 id="finding-nackgammon-title">A new starting position</h2>
-<p class="finding-text">Each model was asked Nackgammon positions and standard positions matched to them. Compared group against group (one group's drop minus another's: decision models, workhorses, frontier), every 99% interval includes 0, so the test does not show the groups' drops to differ. Random play's own drop is −4.6 PR on the main 200 pairs: the Nackgammon positions were slightly easier for random play. Outside the groups, the late entry Base Labs Elephant-1 dropped (+8.66 PR, 97.5% interval +0.42 to +16.02). <strong>Unclear means the test can’t tell, not that the scores are equal.</strong>
